.TH XDG-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "devtools-hub 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xdg-audit \- audit XDG Base Directory paths, fallbacks, and disk usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xdg-audit
.RB [ \-\-strict ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xdg-audit
evaluates standard XDG Base Directory environment variables
.RB ( XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ,
.BR XDG_STATE_HOME ,
and
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ),
verifies directory existence on the local filesystem, and calculates human-readable disk usage via
.BR du (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Return a non-zero exit code if any resolved XDG directory is missing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Audit completed successfully (or all directories present under \-\-strict).
.TP
.B 1
Invalid CLI arguments or missing XDG directories when invoked with \-\-strict.
